{"tool_id": "cli-mcp-server::show_security_rules", "enriched_text": "show_security_rules Show what commands and operations are allowed in this environment.\n", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "google-workspace::list_emails", "enriched_text": "list_emails List recent emails from Gmail inbox Parameters: maxResults, query", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "google-workspace::search_emails", "enriched_text": "search_emails Search emails with advanced query Parameters: query, maxResults", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "google-workspace::send_email", "enriched_text": "send_email Send a new email Parameters: to, subject, body, cc, bcc", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "google-workspace::modify_email", "enriched_text": "modify_email Modify email labels (archive, trash, mark read/unread) Parameters: id, addLabels, removeLabels", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "google-workspace::create_event", "enriched_text": "create_event Create a new calendar event Parameters: summary, location, description, start, end, attendees", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "google-workspace::update_event", "enriched_text": "update_event Update an existing calendar event Parameters: eventId, summary, location, description, start, end, attendees", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "google-workspace::delete_event", "enriched_text": "delete_event Delete a calendar event Parameters: eventId", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "lara-translate::create_memory", "enriched_text": "create_memory Create a translation memory with a custom name in your Lara Translate account. Translation memories store pairs of source and target text segments (translation units) for reuse in future translations. Parameters: name, external_id", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "lara-translate::delete_memory", "enriched_text": "delete_memory Deletes a translation memory from your Lara Translate account. Parameters: id", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "lara-translate::update_memory", "enriched_text": "update_memory Updates a translation memory in your Lara Translate account. Parameters: id, name", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "lara-translate::add_translation", "enriched_text": "add_translation Adds a translation to a translation memory in your Lara Translate account. Parameters: id, source, target, sentence, translation, tuid, sentence_before, sentence_after", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "lara-translate::delete_translation", "enriched_text": "delete_translation Deletes a translation from a translation memory from your Lara Translate account. Parameters: id, source, target, sentence, translation, tuid, sentence_before, sentence_after", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "lara-translate::import_tmx", "enriched_text": "import_tmx Imports a TMX file into a translation memory in your Lara Translate account. Parameters: id, tmx_content, tmx_url, gzip", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "lara-translate::check_import_status", "enriched_text": "check_import_status Checks the status of a TMX file import job in your Lara Translate account. Parameters: id", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "lara-translate::list_memories", "enriched_text": "list_memories Lists all translation memories in your Lara Translate account.", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "mcp-code-executor::initialize_code_file", "enriched_text": "initialize_code_file Create a new Python file with initial content. Use this as the first step for longer code that may exceed token limits. Follow with append_to_code_file for additional code. Parameters: content, filename", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "mcp-code-executor::append_to_code_file", "enriched_text": "append_to_code_file Append content to an existing Python code file. Use this to add more code to a file created with initialize_code_file, allowing you to build up larger code bases in parts. Parameters: file_path, content", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "mcp-code-executor::execute_code_file", "enriched_text": "execute_code_file Execute an existing Python file. Use this as the final step after building up code with initialize_code_file and append_to_code_file. Parameters: file_path", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "mcp-code-executor::install_dependencies", "enriched_text": "install_dependencies Install Python dependencies in the venv-uv environment Parameters: packages", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "mcp-code-executor::check_installed_packages", "enriched_text": "check_installed_packages Check if packages are installed in the venv-uv environment Parameters: packages", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "mcp-code-executor::configure_environment", "enriched_text": "configure_environment Change the environment configuration settings Parameters: type, conda_name, venv_path, uv_venv_path", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "mcp-code-executor::get_environment_config", "enriched_text": "get_environment_config Get the current environment configuration", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "national-parks::getAlerts", "enriched_text": "getAlerts Get current alerts for national parks including closures, hazards, and important information Parameters: parkCode, limit, start, q", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "national-parks::getEvents", "enriched_text": "getEvents Find upcoming events at parks Parameters: parkCode, limit, start, dateStart, dateEnd, q", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "open-library::get_book_cover", "enriched_text": "get_book_cover Get the URL for a book's cover image using a key (ISBN, OCLC, LCCN, OLID, ID) and value. Parameters: key, value, size", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "osm-mcp-server::search_category", "enriched_text": "search_category \nSearch for specific types of places within a defined geographic area.\n\nThis tool allows targeted searches for places matching specific categories within\na rectangular geographic region. It's particularly useful for filtering places by type\n(restaurants, schools, parks, etc.) within a neighborhood or city district. Results include\ncomplete location details and metadata about each matching place.\n\nArgs:\n    category: Main OSM category to search for (e.g., \"amenity\", \"shop\", \"tourism\", \"building\")\n    min_latitude: Southern boundary of search area (decimal degrees)\n    min_longitude: Western boundary of search area (decimal degrees)\n    max_latitude: Northern boundary of search area (decimal degrees)\n    max_longitude: Eastern boundary of search area (decimal degrees)\n    subcategories: Optional list of specific subcategories to filter by (e.g., [\"restaurant\", \"cafe\"])\n    \nReturns:\n    Structured results including:\n    - Query parameters\n    - Count of matching places\n    - List of matching places with coordinates, names, and metadata\n Parameters: category, min_latitude, min_longitude, max_latitude, max_longitude, subcategories", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "osm-mcp-server::suggest_meeting_point", "enriched_text": "suggest_meeting_point \nFind the optimal meeting place for multiple people coming from different locations.\n\nThis tool calculates a central meeting point based on the locations of multiple individuals,\nthen recommends suitable venues near that central point. Ideal for planning social gatherings,\nbusiness meetings, or any situation where multiple people need to converge from different\nstarting points.\n\nArgs:\n    locations: List of dictionaries, each containing the latitude and longitude of a person's location\n              Example: [{\"latitude\": 37.7749, \"longitude\": -122.4194}, {\"latitude\": 37.3352, \"longitude\": -121.8811}]\n    venue_type: Type of venue to suggest as a meeting point. Options include:\n               \"cafe\", \"restaurant\", \"bar\", \"library\", \"park\", etc.\n    \nReturns:\n    Meeting point recommendations including:\n    - Calculated center point coordinates\n    - List of suggested venues with names and details\n    - Total number of matching venues in the area\n Parameters: locations, venue_type", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "osm-mcp-server::explore_area", "enriched_text": "explore_area \nGenerate a comprehensive profile of an area including all amenities and features.\n\nThis powerful analysis tool creates a detailed overview of a neighborhood or area by\nidentifying and categorizing all geographic features, amenities, and points of interest.\nResults are organized by category for easy analysis. Excellent for neighborhood research,\narea comparisons, and location-based decision making.\n\nArgs:\n    latitude: Center point latitude (decimal degrees)\n    longitude: Center point longitude (decimal degrees)\n    radius: Search radius in meters (defaults to 500m)\n    \nReturns:\n    In-depth area profile including:\n    - Address and location context\n    - Total feature count\n    - Features organized by category and subcategory\n    - Each feature includes name, coordinates, and detailed metadata\n Parameters: latitude, longitude, radius", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "osm-mcp-server::find_schools_nearby", "enriched_text": "find_schools_nearby \nLocate educational institutions near a specific location, filtered by education level.\n\nThis specialized search tool identifies schools, colleges, and other educational institutions\nwithin a specified distance from a location. Results can be filtered by education level\n(elementary, middle, high school, university, etc.). Essential for families evaluating\nneighborhoods or real estate purchases with education considerations.\n\nArgs:\n    latitude: Center point latitude (decimal degrees)\n    longitude: Center point longitude (decimal degrees)\n    radius: Search radius in meters (defaults to 2000m/2km)\n    education_levels: Optional list of specific education levels to filter by\n                     (e.g., [\"elementary\", \"secondary\", \"university\"])\n    \nReturns:\n    List of educational institutions with:\n    - Name and type\n    - Distance from search point\n    - Education levels offered\n    - Contact information if available\n    - Other relevant metadata\n Parameters: latitude, longitude, radius, education_levels", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "osm-mcp-server::analyze_commute", "enriched_text": "analyze_commute \nPerform a detailed commute analysis between home and work locations.\n\nThis advanced tool analyzes commute options between two locations (typically home and work),\ncomparing multiple transportation modes and providing detailed metrics for each option.\nIncludes estimated travel times, distances, turn-by-turn directions, and other commute-relevant\ndata. Essential for real estate decisions, lifestyle planning, and workplace relocation analysis.\n\nArgs:\n    home_latitude: Home location latitude (decimal degrees)\n    home_longitude: Home location longitude (decimal degrees)\n    work_latitude: Workplace location latitude (decimal degrees)\n    work_longitude: Workplace location longitude (decimal degrees)\n    modes: List of transportation modes to analyze (options: \"car\", \"foot\", \"bike\")\n    depart_at: Optional departure time (format: \"HH:MM\") for time-sensitive routing\n    \nReturns:\n    Comprehensive commute analysis with:\n    - Summary comparing all transportation modes\n    - Detailed route information for each mode\n    - Total distance and duration for each option\n    - Turn-by-turn directions\n Parameters: home_latitude, home_longitude, work_latitude, work_longitude, modes, depart_at", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "osm-mcp-server::find_parking_facilities", "enriched_text": "find_parking_facilities \nLocate parking facilities near a specific location.\n\nThis tool finds parking options (lots, garages, street parking) near a specified location.\nResults can be filtered by parking type and include capacity information where available.\nUseful for trip planning, city navigation, and evaluating parking availability in urban areas.\n\nArgs:\n    latitude: Center point latitude (decimal degrees)\n    longitude: Center point longitude (decimal degrees)\n    radius: Search radius in meters (defaults to 1000m/1km)\n    parking_type: Optional filter for specific types of parking facilities\n                 (\"surface\", \"underground\", \"multi-storey\", etc.)\n    \nReturns:\n    List of parking facilities with:\n    - Name and type\n    - Capacity information if available\n    - Fee structure if available\n    - Access restrictions\n    - Distance from search point\n Parameters: latitude, longitude, radius, parking_type", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "twelvedata::GetPrice", "enriched_text": "GetPrice This endpoint is a lightweight method that allows retrieving only the real-time price of the selected instrument. Parameters: params", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "twelvedata::GetQuote", "enriched_text": "GetQuote Quote endpoint is an efficient method to retrieve the latest quote of the selected instrument. Parameters: params", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "twelvedata::GetStocks", "enriched_text": "GetStocks This API call returns an array of symbols available at Twelve Data API. This list is updated daily. Parameters: params", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "twelvedata::GetTimeSeriesBBands", "enriched_text": "GetTimeSeriesBBands Bollinger Bands (BBANDS) are volatility bands placed above and below a moving average, measuring price volatility and helping traders identify potential overbought or oversold conditions. Parameters: params", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "twelvedata::GetExchangeRate", "enriched_text": "GetExchangeRate This API call returns real-time exchange rate for currency pair. Works with forex and cryptocurrency. Parameters: params", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "twelvedata::GetTimeSeriesEma", "enriched_text": "GetTimeSeriesEma The Exponential Moving Average (EMA) is a weighted moving average that gives more importance to recent price data, making it more responsive to new information and helping traders identify trends and potential entry or exit points. Parameters: params", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "twelvedata::GetStatistics", "enriched_text": "GetStatistics Returns current overview of company’s main statistics including valuation metrics and financials. Parameters: params", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "twelvedata::GetProfile", "enriched_text": "GetProfile Returns general information about the company. Parameters: params", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "twelvedata::GetMarketState", "enriched_text": "GetMarketState Check the state of all available exchanges, time to open, and time to close. Returns all available stock exchanges by default. Parameters: params", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "twelvedata::GetEod", "enriched_text": "GetEod This endpoint returns the latest End of Day (EOD) price of an instrument. Parameters: params", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "twelvedata::GetTimeSeriesSma", "enriched_text": "GetTimeSeriesSma The Simple Moving Average (SMA) is a smoothing indicator that calculates the average price of a security over a specified period, helping traders identify trends and potential support or resistance levels. Parameters: params", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "twelvedata::GetForexPairs", "enriched_text": "GetForexPairs This API call returns an array of forex pairs available at Twelve Data API. This list is updated daily. Parameters: params", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "twelvedata::GetTimeSeriesAtr", "enriched_text": "GetTimeSeriesAtr The Average True Range (ATR) is a volatility indicator that measures the average range of price movement over a specified period, helping traders assess market volatility. Parameters: params", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "twelvedata::GetDividends", "enriched_text": "GetDividends Returns the amount of dividends paid out for the last 10+ years. Parameters: params", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "twelvedata::GetEarnings", "enriched_text": "GetEarnings This API call returns earnings data for a given company, including EPS estimate and EPS actual. Earnings are available for complete company history. Parameters: params", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "twelvedata::GetCurrencyConversion", "enriched_text": "GetCurrencyConversion This API call returns real-time exchange rate and converted amount for currency pair. Works with forex and cryptocurrency. Parameters: params", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "twelvedata::GetExchanges", "enriched_text": "GetExchanges This API call returns an array of stock or ETF exchanges available at Twelve Data API. This list is updated daily. Parameters: params", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "twelvedata::GetSplits", "enriched_text": "GetSplits Returns the date and the split factor of shares of the company for the last 10+ years. Parameters: params", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "twelvedata::GetEarliestTimestamp", "enriched_text": "GetEarliestTimestamp This method returns the first available DateTime for a given instrument at the specific interval. Parameters: params", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "twelvedata::GetEtf", "enriched_text": "GetEtf This API call returns an array of ETFs available at Twelve Data API. This list is updated daily. Parameters: params", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "twelvedata::GetCommodities", "enriched_text": "GetCommodities This API call returns an array of commodity pairs available at Twelve Data API. This list is updated daily. Parameters: params", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "twelvedata::GetFunds", "enriched_text": "GetFunds This API call returns an array of funds available at Twelve Data API. This list is updated daily. Parameters: params", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "twelvedata::GetIpoCalendar", "enriched_text": "GetIpoCalendar This endpoint returns past, today, or upcoming IPOs. Parameters: params", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "twelvedata::GetCryptocurrencyExchanges", "enriched_text": "GetCryptocurrencyExchanges This API call returns an array of cryptocurrency exchanges available at Twelve Data API. This list is updated daily. Parameters: params", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "twelvedata::GetTimeSeriesCross", "enriched_text": "GetTimeSeriesCross This API call returns meta and cross rate time series for the requested instruments. Metaobject consists of general information about the requested symbol. Time series is the array of objects ordered by time descending with Open, High, Low, Close prices. Works with stocks, forex and cryptocurrency. Parameters: params", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "twelvedata::GetCrossListings", "enriched_text": "GetCrossListings This API call returns an array of cross listed symbols for a specified instrument. Cross listings are the same securities listed on different exchanges. This list is updated daily. Parameters: params", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "twelvedata::GetTechnicalIndicators", "enriched_text": "GetTechnicalIndicators This API call returns an array of objects with available technical indicators. This endpoint might be used to build an abstract interface to make more convenient API calls from the application. Parameters: params", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "twelvedata::GetApiUsage", "enriched_text": "GetApiUsage This endpoint will provide information on the current usage of Twelve Data API. Parameters: params", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "twelvedata::GetLogo", "enriched_text": "GetLogo Returns a logo of company, cryptocurrency, or forex pair. Parameters: params", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "twelvedata::GetTimeSeriesAdx", "enriched_text": "GetTimeSeriesAdx The Average Directional Index (ADX) measures the strength of a trend, regardless of direction, helping traders determine if a market is trending or ranging. Parameters: params", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "weather::get_current_weather", "enriched_text": "get_current_weather Get current weather conditions for a location in the United States. Perfect for 'What's the weather like in [US location]?' questions. Covers all US states, territories, and coastal waters. Parameters: location", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "weather::get_weather_forecast", "enriched_text": "get_weather_forecast Get multi-day weather forecast for a location in the United States. Perfect for 'What's the forecast for [US location]?' questions. Provides detailed day/night forecasts for up to 7 days. Parameters: location, days", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "weather::get_hourly_forecast", "enriched_text": "get_hourly_forecast Get hour-by-hour weather forecast for a location in the United States. Perfect for 'What's the hourly forecast?' or 'Will it rain this afternoon in [US location]?' questions. Provides detailed hourly conditions for up to 48 hours. Parameters: location, hours", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "weather::get_weather_alerts", "enriched_text": "get_weather_alerts Get active weather alerts, warnings, watches, and advisories for locations in the United States. Perfect for 'Are there any weather alerts in [US location]?' questions. Covers severe weather, winter storms, heat warnings, flood alerts, and more. Parameters: location, severity", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "weather::get_local_time", "enriched_text": "get_local_time Get the current local time for a US location. Shows what time it is right now at the specified location. Parameters: location", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "weather-data::weather_current", "enriched_text": "weather_current \nGet current weather for a location.\nArgs:\n    q (str): Location query (city name, lat/lon, postal code, etc).\n    aqi (str): Include air quality data ('yes' or 'no').\nReturns:\n    dict: WeatherAPI current weather JSON.\n Parameters: q, aqi", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "weather-data::weather_forecast", "enriched_text": "weather_forecast \nGet weather forecast (1–14 days) for a location.\nArgs:\n    q (str): Location query (city name, lat/lon, postal code, etc).\n    days (int): Number of days (1–14).\n    aqi (str): Include air quality ('yes' or 'no').\n    alerts (str): Include weather alerts ('yes' or 'no').\nReturns:\n    dict: WeatherAPI forecast JSON.\n Parameters: q, days, aqi, alerts", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "weather-data::weather_alerts", "enriched_text": "weather_alerts \nGet weather alerts for a location.\nArgs:\n    q (str): Location query.\nReturns:\n    dict: WeatherAPI alerts JSON.\n Parameters: q", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "weather-data::weather_airquality", "enriched_text": "weather_airquality \nGet air quality for a location.\nArgs:\n    q (str): Location query.\nReturns:\n    dict: WeatherAPI air quality JSON.\n Parameters: q", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "weather-data::weather_timezone", "enriched_text": "weather_timezone \nGet timezone info for a location.\nArgs:\n    q (str): Location query.\nReturns:\n    dict: WeatherAPI timezone JSON.\n Parameters: q", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "weather-data::weather_sports", "enriched_text": "weather_sports \nGet sports events (e.g., football, cricket) for a location.\nArgs:\n    q (str): Location query.\nReturns:\n    dict: WeatherAPI sports JSON.\n Parameters: q", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "whois::whois_tld", "enriched_text": "whois_tld Looksup whois information about the Top Level Domain (TLD) Parameters: tld", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "whois::whois_ip", "enriched_text": "whois_ip Looksup whois information about the IP Parameters: ip", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "whois::whois_as", "enriched_text": "whois_as Looksup whois information about the Autonomous System Number (ASN) Parameters: asn", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "wikipedia::summarize_article_for_query", "enriched_text": "summarize_article_for_query Get a summary of a Wikipedia article tailored to a specific query. Parameters: title, query, max_length", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "wikipedia::summarize_article_section", "enriched_text": "summarize_article_section Get a summary of a specific section of a Wikipedia article. Parameters: title, section_title, max_length", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "wikipedia::get_related_topics", "enriched_text": "get_related_topics Get topics related to a Wikipedia article based on links and categories. Parameters: title, limit", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "wikipedia::get_sections", "enriched_text": "get_sections Get the sections of a Wikipedia article. Parameters: title", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "wikipedia::get_links", "enriched_text": "get_links Get the links contained within a Wikipedia article. Parameters: title", "method": "rule"}
{"tool_id": "exa::web_search_exa", "enriched_text": "This tool performs real-time web searches, providing optimized results and extracting relevant content from the web. Users utilize this tool when they need to find information or content from the internet quickly. web search real-time content extraction", "method": "llm"}
{"tool_id": "mongodb::find", "enriched_text": "Executes a find query to retrieve documents from a MongoDB collection based on specified criteria. This tool is used when a user needs to search for specific documents within a MongoDB database. database retrieve query MongoDB search", "method": "llm"}
{"tool_id": "mongodb::aggregate", "enriched_text": "This tool runs an aggregation operation on a MongoDB collection to process and analyze data. Use this tool when there is a need to summarize or transform data within a MongoDB collection. mongodb aggregation data processing analysis collection", "method": "llm"}
{"tool_id": "mongodb::count", "enriched_text": "Counts the total number of documents present in a specified MongoDB collection. This tool is used when a user needs to determine the size of a collection in MongoDB. mongodb count documents collection database", "method": "llm"}
{"tool_id": "mongodb::list-databases", "enriched_text": "This tool lists all databases associated with a MongoDB connection. Use this tool when there is a need to view all available databases in a MongoDB instance. mongodb list databases connection view", "method": "llm"}
{"tool_id": "mongodb::list-collections", "enriched_text": "This tool lists all collections within a specified database, providing an overview of the data structure. Use this tool when needing to view the collections available in a specific database. database list collections mongodb overview", "method": "llm"}
{"tool_id": "mongodb::collection-schema", "enriched_text": "This tool describes the schema for a collection in a MongoDB database, outlining the structure and organization of data within that collection. Use this tool when needing to understand the data structure of a specific MongoDB collection. database describe schema MongoDB collection", "method": "llm"}
{"tool_id": "oxylabs::oxylabs_scraper", "enriched_text": "This tool utilizes the Oxylabs Web Scraper API to extract data from websites, offering features such as JavaScript rendering, structured data parsing, and HTML output in Markdown format. Use this tool when there is a need to scrape data from websites that require JavaScript rendering or when structured data extraction is required. web scraping data extraction JavaScript rendering structured data HTML output", "method": "llm"}
{"tool_id": "airtable::list_records", "enriched_text": "This tool retrieves and displays records from a designated Airtable table based on specified criteria. Use this tool when there is a need to access and view records from a specific table in Airtable. Airtable retrieve list filter records", "method": "llm"}
{"tool_id": "airtable::search_records", "enriched_text": "This tool searches for records in a specified table that contain a given text within designated fields. Use this tool when needing to locate specific records based on text criteria in a database. database search text records Airtable", "method": "llm"}
{"tool_id": "airtable::list_bases", "enriched_text": "This tool retrieves and displays all accessible bases within Airtable, providing users with an overview of their available data structures. Use this tool when needing to view or manage the bases available in an Airtable account. Airtable list retrieve bases data", "method": "llm"}
{"tool_id": "airtable::list_tables", "enriched_text": "This tool retrieves a list of all tables within a specified base in Airtable, providing an overview of the available data structures. Use this tool when needing to view the tables contained in a specific Airtable base. Airtable list tables baseId detailLevel", "method": "llm"}
{"tool_id": "calculator::calculate", "enriched_text": "This tool calculates and evaluates the provided mathematical expression. Use this tool when there is a need to compute the result of a specific mathematical expression. mathematics calculate evaluate expression computation", "method": "llm"}
{"tool_id": "fetch::fetch_markdown", "enriched_text": "This tool fetches the content of a specified website and converts it into Markdown format for easier readability and formatting. Use this tool when there is a need to retrieve and format website content for documentation or further processing. web fetch content Markdown format", "method": "llm"}
{"tool_id": "git::git_status", "enriched_text": "This tool displays the current status of the working tree in a version control system, indicating changes that have been staged, modified, or are untracked. It is used when a user needs to check the state of their files in the repository. version control status working tree file changes repository", "method": "llm"}
{"tool_id": "git::git_diff_unstaged", "enriched_text": "This tool displays the differences between the current working directory and the last committed state, highlighting changes that have not yet been staged for the next commit. Use this tool when a user wants to review modifications made in the working directory before staging them. version control view changes unstaged repository", "method": "llm"}
{"tool_id": "git::git_log", "enriched_text": "This tool displays the commit logs from a version control repository, providing a chronological record of changes made to the codebase. Use this tool when needing to review the history of commits in a project. version control view commit logs repository", "method": "llm"}
{"tool_id": "git::git_show", "enriched_text": "This tool displays the contents of a specific commit in a version control system, providing insights into changes made at that point in time. Use this tool when needing to review the details of a particular commit in a repository. version control view commit repository changes", "method": "llm"}
{"tool_id": "slack::conversations_history", "enriched_text": "This tool retrieves messages from a specified channel using the channel ID, allowing users to access historical conversations. This tool is used when a user needs to obtain past messages from a specific channel. communication retrieve messages channel_id history", "method": "llm"}
